{% extends 'email/_base.html.twig' %}

{% block emailTitle %}Registration Completed GEWIS{% endblock %}
{% block preheader %}{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}Update on your registration{% endblock %}
{% block subheading %}You have been confirmed as member of GEWIS!{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
    <p>Dear {{ firstName }},</p>
    <p>
        First of all, welcome, and thank you for your registration at GEWIS. From tomorrow on, your membership number will
        be {{ lidnr }}.<br>
        You can use this membership number to log in to the website, where you can, among other things, subscribe to
        activities and look at photos from all the fun activities that you, together with the other members, have
        experienced. Below more information on all the functions of the website can be found, but first of all, you can
        activate your account for the website using the following link:
        <a href="https://gewis.nl/user/activate" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">gewis.nl/user/activate</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        Besides getting access to the website, you can also create a SudoSOS account, our system with which you will be
        able to buy drinks from the refrigerators and sweets you can find on the bar. You will need this account if you
        want to get a drink at the weekly social drink (usually called the &ldquo;borrel&rdquo;). To do this, first, log in
        to the GEWIS website using the account created above. After this, go to
        <a href="https://sudosos.gewis.nl" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">sudosos.gewis.nl</a>.
        When you log in for the first time, you will have to read and accept the terms and conditions. After that, you can
        also set a pin code to use the point of sales on your own.
    </p>
    <p>
        With kind regards,
        <br>The board of GEWIS
    </p>
    
        {% macro section(title) %}
            <hr style="color: #F2F2F2;"/>
            <p style="font-size: 18px; text-align: center; font-weight: bolder; margin-bottom: 6px;">{{ title }}</p>
        {% endmacro %}
        
        {% import _self as welcome %}
        
        <p>
            You might have noticed that GEWIS has its own website, but that it might not be as easy to access as you had
            hoped. Fear not, as this instruction mail should help you in no time! There are several different tabs in which
            you can find the following information:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <b>Association</b>: If you have ever wondered who is actively helping the association by means of organizing
                activities, taking pictures, or publishing the association magazine: take a look at this page! All our
                committees, fraternities, and sororities are listed here. Besides that, you can take a look if you forgot what
                your board looks like, or how you should sing the GEWIS song ;)
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Companies</b>: At some point in the future, you could be looking for an internship or a graduation project
                from a company. At this header, you find a list of numerous companies offering vacancies for members of GEWIS.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Education</b>: Especially important when the exam weeks are coming near, here you can find all the old
                exams and summaries that GEWIS has available for the courses of Mathematics and Computer Science. You can also
                order your books from here, or submit a complaint about a teacher or a course.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Activities</b>: Besides studying, it is of course important to relax and enjoy your student life every once
                in a while. Here, you find an overview of all the activities GEWIS organizes: from weekends to lunch lectures,
                from external activities such as a conference to internal activities such as a bridge course. Don&rsquo;t
                forget that most activities require you to subscribe in advance and that some activities are full quite fast!
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Photos</b>: This kind of speaks for itself: at nearly every activity, members of GEFLITST (the photo
                committee of GEWIS) are busy taking pictures of our members. If you&rsquo;re scrolling through the photos,
                don&rsquo;t forget to tag the members you know in the picture! This week's photos will be on the website
                already so check for them regularly :)
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>Members</b>: In this section, you can find plenty of different important shortcuts to other parts of the
                website. For example; you can look at an overview of your profile, look up fellow member, see when the next
                General Members Meeting (GMM) is, access your SudoSOS account with which you can buy drinks and food (you have
                to agree to the terms of use before you can buy stuff), and many other shortcuts. Be sure to check it out! And
                of course, on our homepage, you can find numerous of these sections in short. A few of the upcoming events,
                the birthdays of today, the photo of the week, a poll, and of course random infima. So as you can see,
                there&rsquo;s a lot to see and do on our website, so be sure to check it out every once in a while!
            </li>
        </ul>
        {{ welcome.section('First-year committees') }}
        <p>
            GEWIS has many committees and fraternities, and we even set up committees specifically for first-year students! As
            an upcoming student, you can join an FYC (First-Year Committee) to get a taste of what it's like to be an active
            member at GEWIS. Together with your fellow first-year students, you will be fleshing out your own identity by
            creating a logo and custom clothing. Then you can organize fun activities for the association and collaborate with
            other committees or fraternities!<br><br>
            To join a first year committee information meeting, you can subscribe to
            <a href="https://gew.is/fycinterest" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">this activity</a>!
        </p>
        {{ welcome.section('Ordering books') }}
        <p>
            By becoming a GEWIS member you have the right to a specialized discount! By navigating to
            <a href="https://gewis.nl/books" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">gewis.nl/books</a>
            you can find your study and see which books will be used for your courses.
        </p>
        {{ welcome.section('GEWIS on social media') }}
        {# The shared layout has no social icons in its footer, so the accounts the old footer linked to are named here
           instead of being referred to as "see below". #}
        <p>
            Next to our own photo section on the website, you can also find us on social media. We have
            <a href="https://www.instagram.com/svgewis" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Instagram</a>,
            <a href="https://www.facebook.com/svgewis" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Facebook</a>,
            and
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/study-association-gewis/" style="color: #C40000; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">LinkedIn</a>.
            Additionally, we have a weekly newsletter, for which you are automatically subscribed. You will get your first
            newsletter soon!
        </p>
{% endblock %}
{% block footerNote %}You received this email because you registered as a member of GEWIS and your membership was confirmed. This is a one-time mailing to update you about the status of your request.{% endblock %}
